# Line-ending policy for the agent-workflow surface (Mason, 2026-07-13).
#
# `scripts/sync-agent-workflows.mjs` regenerates the Codex adapter files under
# `.agents/` from the `.claude/` sources and compares them; its `--write` path
# emits Unix (LF) line endings for every file it writes.
# `scripts/check-agent-workflows.mjs` and `scripts/agent-health-check.mjs` both
# reach that same comparison rather than implementing their own.
#
# Why the pin exists: on Windows checkouts `core.autocrlf=true` was rewriting
# these files to CRLF, so the check reported them "stale" (identical text,
# different line endings) and blocked every commit. Pinning both the sources the
# generator reads and the targets it writes to LF keeps the committed form
# canonical on every platform.
#
# The pin is not the only defense, because it governs what Git stores, not what
# sits on disk. A file can be CRLF in the working tree and still hash identically
# to its LF blob, which makes it invisible to `git diff`. Both mirror comparisons
# therefore ignore line endings — the generator since 2026-07-16 (#147),
# `agent-health` since 2026-08-19 — via `scripts/normalize-eol.mjs`. A mismatch in
# any OTHER byte is still a real failure.
.agents/**          text eol=lf
.claude/skills/**   text eol=lf
.claude/commands/** text eol=lf
.husky/**           text eol=lf
.github/workflows/** text eol=lf
*.sh                 text eol=lf

